Your description seems wrong to me.  Can you explain how to replicate
your problem?  My first inclination is to believe that you're just
mistaken.

If you pick up items and they don't stack, it's because they had a
different identified status, different characteristics (BUC status,
greased/fireproof/etc, enchantment), different payment status (either
some are paid and some aren't, or several are unpaid but differ on the
surcharge), or they're not stackable items (swords, wands, etc).

If you pick something up that hasn't stacked with other items and
wasn't unpaid, drop it, and pick it up again then it won't stack unless
there was another step in between (identifying it, BUC identifying it,
cancelling/enchanting it, etc).

As I mentioned, this is easy to check in wizard mode.  You can also
read through invent.c to see the code logic.



